    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.2.03-02",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Demographic effects can include changes in mortality and life expectancy where illness causes premature deaths. If losses affect particular ages, the age structure and household composition can change. However, a population pyramid gap alone does not prove an HIV effect; migration, past births, other health conditions or recording can contribute. Relevant age-specific health and demographic data are needed to support attribution.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.2.03-1",
        "CL-6137-3.2.03-2",
        "CL-6137-3.2.03-01-1",
        "CL-6137-3.2.03-01-2",
