    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.2.03-03",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Mortality and fertility interact with total growth. Reduced deaths through treatment can support survival and change the population trajectory. This does not establish an exact national growth rate without births and migration as well. A general mechanism should not be turned into a precise prediction from one treatment statistic. Nor should a greater number living with HIV be interpreted automatically as worsening mortality.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.2.03-1",
        "CL-6137-3.2.03-2",
        "CL-6137-3.2.03-01-1",
        "CL-6137-3.2.03-01-2",
