    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.2.03-09",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Health spending has immediate costs and possible wider benefits. Funding treatment, prevention and support requires resources, while healthier people can continue learning, working and caring for others. A narrow account of medicines as an economic cost misses those benefits. Conversely, a statement that treatment saves money needs a defined period and complete relevant cost evidence rather than an assumed amount.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.2.03-1",
        "CL-6137-3.2.03-2",
        "CL-6137-3.2.03-01-1",
        "CL-6137-3.2.03-01-2",
