    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.2.03-10",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A hypothetical household account illustrates one pathway without assigning it to a real family. During an illness interval, earnings fall from N$3,000 to N$2,000 while relevant travel and care costs rise by N$400. Available funds for other needs are N$1,400 lower than before if all other flows are unchanged. This arithmetic describes the supplied scenario, not a usual loss experienced by every household or proof of an individual's diagnosis.",
