    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.2.03-13",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Economic impacts concern money, work and production. Illness and deaths reduce the number of skilled and experienced workers, so firms lose productivity and must recruit and train replacements. Absenteeism rises, household incomes and savings fall, and fewer people pay tax. Government spends more on health care, medicines and grants, leaving less for other development. Treatment reduces many of these effects by keeping people healthy enough to work.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.2.03-1",
        "CL-6137-3.2.03-2",
        "CL-6137-3.2.03-01-1",
        "CL-6137-3.2.03-01-2",
